    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on several favorable matchups today, led by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest daily efficiency score of 82.40. His prime position atop the order against Cade Cavalli, combined with an optimal platoon advantage, positions him as the engine of our offense. Following closely is **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56), whose matchup against Chris Bassitt benefits from a significant dynamic platoon boost, making him a critical start for both R and SB production. We also see high upside in the outfield, where **Heliot Ramos** (66.96) and **Kyle Tucker** (66.58) provide strong floors. **Heliot Ramos** is bolstered by a park factor increase and a favorable matchup against Luis Severino, while **Kyle Tucker** gains an extra edge from wind conditions blowing out against Jos\u00e9 Soriano, reinforcing his status as a cornerstone of the lineup.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved the bench, where **Nolan Schanuel** (50.80) was the final player left out of the starting nine. While **Nolan Schanuel** projected well, he was squeezed out by the tactical necessity of slotting in **Nasim Nunez** and **Brady House** to maintain our competitive edge in the scarcity-driven stolen base category. Though the optimizer favored their utility, we must remain cautious of the risks inherent in our \"Lineup Pending\" status; if **Liam Hicks** or **Drake Baldwin** are shifted significantly down their respective batting orders, their efficiency scores will likely see a downward correction. Furthermore, we are keeping a close watch on **Jackson Merrill**, whose 52.65 score is suppressed by a difficult clash with Logan Gilbert; he remains in the lineup due to his high-leverage leadoff potential, but he represents our most volatile start against a top-tier pitcher.",
